Domain: Pizzas
  Put toppings on a pizza and sell it to a customer.
  This is a supporting domain

Aggregate: Order
  An order that gathers toppings on a pizza and is eventually sold to a customer.

  An order is identified by its name.

  It has:
    a name: pizza name
    a pizza: pizza
    some toppings: list of topping
    a customer name: customer name, optional

  A pizza name has a value: text, matching "[^ \t\n\r]".
    Rule "a pizza is named" holds when the value is not empty

  A price has:
    a cents: whole number
    Rule "a price is never negative" holds when the cents is at least 0

  A customer name has a value: text, matching "[^ \t\n\r]".
    Rule "a customer is named" holds when the value is not empty

  A topping name has a value: text, matching "[^ \t\n\r]".
    Rule "a topping is named" holds when the value is not empty
    Rule "a topping name is more than whitespace" holds when this is true: !value.to_s.strip.empty?

  A topping amount has a value: whole number.
    Rule "an amount is positive" holds when this is true: value.positive?

  A topping has:
    a name: text, matching "[^ \t\n\r]"
    an amount: whole number

  A size is one of: small and large.

  A pizza has:
    a price cents: price
    a size: size

  Lifecycle: status, starting as available
    Purchase moves an order from available to sold
    Mark terminal: sold

  Command: Create Pizza
    Goal: Put a new pizza on the menu
    Who: Chef
    When a name and a pizza are given
    Then the name and the pizza are set
    And PizzaCreated is announced

  Command: Add Topping
    Goal: Customize a pizza with an ingredient
    Who: Chef
    It can only happen from available
    It acts on an existing order
    It takes:
      a topping: topping name
      an amount: topping amount
    Given "at most 10 toppings" holds when this is true: toppings.size < 10
    Then a row is added to the toppings with name from the topping, amount from the amount
    And ToppingAdded is announced

  Command: Purchase
    Goal: Buy the pizza
    Who: Customer
    It can only happen from available
    It acts on an existing order
    It takes:
      an amount: price
      a customer name: customer name, optional
    Given "a pizza needs at least one topping" holds when this is true: toppings.size.positive?
    Given "a payment was actually made" holds when this is true: amount.cents.positive?
    Given "the payment covers the price" holds when this is true: amount.cents >= pizza.price_cents.cents
    Then the customer name is set
    And PizzaPurchased is announced

  Query: Available
    Where the status is available
    Ordered by name, ascending

  Query: Everything

  Query: By Price
    Ordered by pizza.price_cents.cents, ascending

  Query: By Price Descending
    Ordered by pizza.price_cents.cents, descending

  Query: By Customer
    Ordered by customer_name.value, ascending

  Query: By Customer Descending
    Ordered by customer_name.value, descending

  Query: By Customer Unset Last
    Ordered by customer_name.value, ascending
    Empty values come last

  Query: Costing Less Than
    It takes:
      a ceiling: price
    Where the pizza.price_cents.cents is less than the ceiling
    Ordered by name, ascending

  Query: Expensive
    Where the pizza.price_cents.cents is more than 1000
    Ordered by name, ascending

Policy: On Pizza Payment Received
  Whenever PizzaPaymentReceived is announced by an order
  Then Purchase runs
